{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/959287-just-what-are-the-requirements-for-the-new-dawn","id":959287,"title":"Just what ARE the requirements for the New Dawn?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-28T08:57:49-07:00","id":959287,"title":"Just what ARE the requirements for the New Dawn?","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">I am having the hardest time making sense of just <i>what</i> exactly the requirements are for completing the Pilgrimage. Different sections of the book seem to imply different things. Primarily, I'm confused as to just how many Refinements and/or Roles a character needs to go through.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Page 177</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Each Promethean has a specific path through the Refinements, though the character doesn\u2019t know what it is. The player, however, is well aware of his character\u2019s path. He can drive her to greater success \u2014 or show her greater challenges. In order to complete the Great Work, a character has to internalize lessons from at least <b>four</b> <b>Refinements</b> \u2014 two basic Refinements and two complex Refinements.<br /> [...]<br /> Though it may seem easier to complete a Pilgrimage based on few Refinements rather than all ten, that\u2019s not the case. The Promethean has to complete<b> the same number of Roles</b> either way. Taking in eight or ten Refinements means changing between disparate Roles, going from a Hermit to a Leader to an Ascetic, which means greater changes in the character\u2019s outlook and facets of her personality. Fewer Refinements means the character must take on more Roles from them, giving the character greater consistency at the expense of mystical experience. Each Role provides internal alchemical components for the Magnum Opus, thus its success is based on he number of Roles completed, not the number of Refinements hat the Created studied. Studying <b>more Refinements does give </b><b>her a broader choice</b> when she undergoes the New Dawn <span style=\"color:#433471\">(p. 303)</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Page 186</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">In order to attempt the Magnum Opus, a Promethean must complete at least <b>eight Roles</b>, including at least <b>one Role in every </b><b>Refinement that is on her Pilgrimage</b>. Any Roles not related to her Pilgrimage do not count towards this transformation</span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>New Dawn Modifiers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">0 The character has completed <b>ten Roles</b> related to her Pilgrimage.<br /> \u20131 The character has completed <b>nine Roles</b> related to her Pilgrimage.<br /> \u20132 The character has completed <b>eight Roles</b> related to her Pilgrimage.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Page 186, continued</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In game terms, the exact results depend on the number of <b>Refinements</b> that the character has completed. If the character has completed <b>six or more Refinements</b>, the player can choose whether her character remembers her experiences, or remembers her human life. The character retains all of her Attributes and Skills as a human being and has an Integrity trait equal to the number of <b>Refinements</b> she has completed</div> </div> </div> </div>The chart on page 187 is also based on <b>Refinements</b> completed, going from 4 to 10 with no mention of <b>Roles</b>. So far it seems that while you could go Leader\u2192Companion\u2192Martyr\u2192Exemplar\u2192Confessor\u2192Provoca teur\u2192Psychopomp\u2192Whip, you get a better ending if you go through at least one Role in each of the ten Refinements. The problem comes with the fact that each character has a <i>specific</i> path through the Refinements. While, obviously, each player can choose to go through all ten Refinements, that mechanic implies that some Prometheans are basically screwed from the outset, and can never become a human with more than Integrity 4 and horrible nightmares. In the Storyteller Chapter in the section on Pilgrimage creation, we're even given a sample of the Roles/Refinements that Seeda is intended to go through. </span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><img src=\"https://vgy.me/gVRjk8.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">She completes only seven Refinements, but later during the Example of a New Dawn on page she at least <i>seems</i> like she achieved around the 8-9 area, considering the strong social connections she's got. If not, though, that means Milly's character (not Ava's, as the graphic says) was essentially locked out of the &quot;best&quot; ending from the start. This is mostly a concern because one of my players wants to shoot for that 10-Refinements best ending but for whatever reason really dislikes Argentum from a thematic standpoint (and isn't <i>that</i> fond of Phosphorum). Is the fact that some Prometheans are just doomed to eventually become Integrity 4 emotional messes something I'll just have to deal with if I want to play &quot;by the book&quot;?<br /> <br /> As an aside, but in more than a few places it implies that you need to complete Roles within the Refinements on your Pilgrimage (i.e. the predetermined ones), most notably shown by the sample Pilgrimage chart there having checkboxes next to the Refinement and only lines to write in the Roles (I'm not sure why, as they each have only the three). But it doesn't seem that completing <i>a</i> Role within the Refinement actually matters. If Seeda were to complete the Companion or Servant or Provocateur Role, it wouldn't further her Pilgrimage, except as any other non-Superlative Milestone. One of the things that prompted me to make this thread is that after I'm trying to make a version of that chart that keeps track of which Roles have been completed, and will eventually have a section for the other Milestones.</span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><img src=\"https://vgy.me/ZiMDQH.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></span></div> <br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">It's far from finished, but writing the explanation of how to track your Roles, I realized that I'm not 100% sure how it works.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Also, </span></span><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> might as well ping you, since you're the one who was saying you wished there was a version of that chart in the first place.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> It's also been brought to my attention that it could be read that completing a Refinement requires completing at least one Role, and that completing a Role in a Refinement <i><b>not</b></i> on your Pilgrimage can still add to the number of Refinements you've completed; it's only the <b>Roles</b> that are predetermined, though I'm not sure what gameplay or narrative significance there is in that.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 08-28-2016, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T09:08:43-07:00","id":959292,"title":"","content":"I agree that it seems the rules could be cleaned up some. I got the impression that &quot;completeing a Refinement&quot; means completeing all three roles within, which would mean a minimum of what.. 12 roles? If each Refinement is completed with just ONE Refinement, that seems to suggest you need to complete four refinements, and thus four roles, plus at least four extra Roles. I am hoping the final editting clarifies this considerably. Thankfully, my one Promethean player wants to remember as much as shi can, so shi will need all ten refinements. But even that's a good question--does 1 Role on a Pilgrimage refinement complete that necessity, or is it all three?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T09:19:22-07:00","id":959298,"title":"","content":"The one thing I <i>am</i> mostly certain on is that having a Refinement under your belt only requires you to complete one Role. Otherwise Seeda wouldn't have completed <i>any</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","d